{{Top}}
{{Rhere|Ship|other uses [[Ship (disambiguation)|Ship]]}}
{{Quote|I've outrun Imperial starships, not the local bulk cruisers, mind you. I'm talking about the big Corellian ships now.|[[Han Solo]]|<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref>}}
[[File:Various_ships-SWU.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Various starship models, including three [[Allanar N3 light freighter]]s, in flight]]
A '''starship''', often referred to as simply a '''ship''', was a manned vehicle used for [[Spacefaring|traveling]] in [[realspace]] or [[hyperspace]]. Dating back [[Millennium|thousands]] of [[Standard year|years]], the earliest starships transported [[spacer]]s to new [[Planet|worlds]] through [[Carbon-freezing|cryogenic freezing]] processes.<ref name="Beware">''[[Return of the Jedi: Beware the Power of the Dark Side!]]''</ref> Upon the invention of the [[hyperdrive]], those that were equipped could travel faster than light by entering hyperspace, drastically reducing the journey times between two [[Star system|solar systems]].<ref name="TSWB">''[[The Star Wars Book]]''</ref>

Due to the complex nature of ships, a variety of power sources were required to maintain and operate essential functions on board. The most common power sources were chemical, fission, or fusion [[reactor]]s, which consumed a variety of fuels based on local resources, and dated back to the [[Galactic Republic|Republic's]] earliest [[Standard day|days]]. Many large ships opted for fusion systems that contained [[hypermatter]]-annihilation cores, which could generate vast amounts of power. Despite all the benefits, most power systems required fuel hazardous to [[Species|organic beings]], often circulating in ship systems as corrosive liquids or combustible and poisonous gases.<ref name="Cross">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: Incredible Cross-Sections]]''</ref> At least some starships possessed [[safety protocols]] built into the [[computer]] system that prevented the [[pilot]] from taking dangerous and reckless actions, though these could be disabled.<ref name="snare">''[[Adventures in Wild Space: The Snare]]''</ref>

Individual starships were registered with the [[Bureau of Ships and Services]] (BoSS), an organization founded millennia before the [[Clone Wars]] responsible for maintaining ship registrations, [[Identification Friend or Foe transponder|transponders]], and pilots' licenses.<ref name="Rise">''[[Rise of the Separatists]]''</ref> The [[Corellian Engineering Corporation]],<ref name="Cross" /> [[Kuat Drive Yards]],<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> [[Sienar Fleet Systems]],<ref name="Art Attack">{{Rebels|Art Attack}}</ref> [[Incom Corporation]], and [[Mon Calamari Shipyards]]<ref name="USW" /> were major manufacturers of starships.

Types of starships included the [[shuttle]], [[transport]], [[freighter]], [[yacht]],<ref name="Episode I">{{Film|I}}</ref> [[scout ship]],<ref name="Kay's Curse">{{Resistance|Kaz's Curse}}</ref> [[starfighter]],<ref name="Episode I" /> [[warship]],<ref name="Episode IV" /> [[hospital ship]],<ref name="TRF">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref> and [[space station]].<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

==Characteristics==
[[File:DarkInk-HothEvacuation.png|thumb|left|300px|Starfighters and larger transports fly over [[Hoth]] as capital ships take fire from the surface during the [[Battle of Hoth]]<ref name="Episode V">''[[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back]]''</ref>]]
A starship's first and foremost purpose was to ferry its occupants through the void of [[Realspace|space]].<ref name="Episode IV" /> For this purpose, starships were covered with an [[Atmosphere|atmospherically]] sealed [[hull]]<ref name="Complete new">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref> and protected from space-borne debris<ref name="Episode IV" /> and [[radiation]]<ref name="Cross" /> by [[deflector shield]]s.<ref name="Episode IV" /> To enter and exit a starship, its occupants had to use pressurized gates called [[airlock]]s; these took the form of hatches or doors in the hull.<ref name="Secret Cargo">{{Rebels|Secret Cargo}}</ref> Finally, to allow passengers to occupy the starship comfortably, most models were equipped with [[life support]] systems which converted the air,<ref name="The Cold">''[[Adventures in Wild Space: The Cold]]''</ref> ambient temperature,<ref name="Force Collector">''[[Force Collector]]''</ref> and pressure inside the hull to levels survivable by most [[species]].<ref name="ROUVG">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref>

To propel themselves through space starships were equipped with [[engine]]s, more specifically [[sublight engine]]s, which worked by burning and expelling [[fuel]] from the starship's fuel tank or by mixing exotic components from an onboard [[reactor]].<ref name="MFOWM">''[[YT-1300 Millennium Falcon Owners' Workshop Manual]]''</ref> More complex drives, such as the [[twin ion engine]], utilized accelerated [[Ion cannon|ion]]s and other subatomic particles.<ref name="TFOWM">''[[TIE Fighter Owners' Workshop Manual]]''</ref><ref name="RSOWM">''[[Rebel Starfighters Owners' Workshop Manual]]''</ref> Some starships were also equipped with a [[hyperdrive]], which allowed the craft to enter [[hyperspace]] and travel a greater distance in less time,<ref name="DB hyperdrive">{{Databank|hyperdrive|Hyperdrive}}</ref> while also requiring the use of a [[navigation computer]] to safely guide the ship through pre-charted [[hyperspace route]]s.<ref name="MFOWM" /> Finally, an important but often overlooked component of every space-borne vessel was the [[gyrocomputer]], which utilized [[control momentum gyroscope]]s to provide a location reference while in the absence of [[planet]]ary terrain.<ref name="BMF 25">{{BuildFalconCite|25|Secrets of Spaceflight}}</ref>

There were as many starship types as there were professions in the [[galaxy]]. These types were separated into classes, primarily denoting the starship's purpose (e.g., [[starfighter]], [[transport]], [[freighter]]) as well as the [[Anaxes War College System]], which classified ships according to their size (e.g., [[corvette]], [[frigate]], [[battlecruiser]]).<ref name="Battles that Changed the Galaxy">''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]''</ref> A starship's class affected its build; for example, combat-focused classes, such as starfighters, included built-in weapons, such as [[laser cannon]]s, and typically lacked a hyperdrive,<ref name="Star Wars Complete New">''[[Star Wars Complete Vehicles, New Edition]]''</ref> while freighters were equipped with larger [[reactor]]s and engines to more efficiently carry heavier cargo.

Starship components included [[repulsorlift]]s,<ref name="Cross" /> [[artificial gravity]],<ref name="dark">''[[Adventures in Wild Space: The Dark]]''</ref> [[deflector shields]], [[hull]]s,<ref name="Episode IV" /> [[sublight engine]]s,<ref name="Builders">''[[Star Wars Builders: Starfighters]]''</ref> [[navigation computer]]s,<ref name="MFOWM" /> [[gyrocomputer]],<ref name="BMF 25" /> [[hyperdrive]]s,<ref name="DB hyperdrive" /> [[life support]],<ref name="ROUVG" /> [[acceleration compensator]]s, [[reactor]]s,<ref name="Cross" /> [[blaster cannon]]s, [[laser cannon]]s,<ref name="Complete Vehicles 2018">[[Star Wars: Complete Vehicles (2018)|''Star Wars: Complete Vehicles'' (2018)]]</ref> [[turbolaser]]s,<ref name="Star Wars Complete New" /> [[missile]]s,<ref name="TVE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> [[sensor]]s,<ref name="MFOWM" /> [[flight computer]]s, [[tractor beam]]s,<ref name="Cross" /> [[airlock]]s,<ref name="Secret Cargo" /> [[docking tube]]s,<ref name="The Rebellion Begins">''[[The Rebellion Begins]]''</ref> [[hangar]]s<ref name="Episode III">''[[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith]]''</ref> and [[escape pod]]s.<ref name="SWEOSAOV">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles]]''</ref>

[[Carbon-freezing]] was once a critical part of a starship, before the invention of the hyperdrive.<ref name="Beware" />

